<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="42f992a0">In a similar way to the original benefits identification, any new benefits should be documented at a high-level so that
they can be reviewed. At this stage, it may be necessary to gather some additional information to help quantify the
benefits. All new benefits should be reviewed by program/project leadership to confirm if they should be classified
formally as a benefit. Once the new benefits has been reviewed and their inclusion into the program/project approved, the
Benefits Register should be updated.&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
